From 7cd157efe1d02926300c32630e5c8d6606278a78 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sunrisepeak <speakshen@163.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 03:59:20 +0900
Subject: [clangd] Completion waits for modules a bounded time

In a file that imports modules, completion waited for the file's first
preamble without limit, and built a module the draft newly imports
synchronously: while a project's modules were being prepared, completion
waited for all of them (minutes on a large Windows project), where stock
clangd answers from its fallback at once.

The first preamble is now waited for up to FirstPreambleWait (600 ms,
--completion-first-preamble-wait-ms; TUScheduler's StaleWithin), past which
completion answers as without a preamble. A newly imported module is waited
for up to CodeCompleteOptions::ModuleWait (250 ms, --completion-module-wait-ms),
as a dependency edit already was, past which the answer comes from the
modules the preamble carries. Either answer is marked incomplete, so the
client asks again and gets the imported names once they are there; the
builds go on meanwhile.
